 "changesFromC1009": [
  "The two CJC-1295 (No DAC) + Ipamorelin blends, which C1-009 left out until the component name was settled. KAN-59/11972 settled it: a blend's printed component names must reconstruct that row's own variant label exactly, so the component is CJC-1295 (No DAC), as this row's label spells it. The corrected facts file changes only these two records; the 14 records C1-009 uses are byte-identical in it.",
  "build_c1.py, xr_compose.py, svg_label_render.py, wpf_kern.ps1 and verify_c1.py are byte-identical to C1-009's copies. c1_variants.py adds only the reference of the corrected facts (KAN-59/11972). write_manifest.py records this batch's claim reference and this note. The kern table covers the strings in this batch.",
  "2 of 2 records have form-neutral label facts: they state the name, the components with their amounts, the product code and the classification, and no form. For those records the printed vial and the per-vial amount basis rest on the packaging declaration alone; labelFacts keeps the hold note and formBasis cites the declaration."
